IMPORT prelude

-- Road Traffic Act 1974 (Western Australia), Part V Division 1, with the rules of the Road Traffic Code 2000, the Road
-- Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Regulations 2014, the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Regulations 2014 and the Road Traffic
-- (Administration) Regulations 2014 that the rider's and the driver's questions turn on -- where I may ride an electric
-- rideable device and how fast, what my speeding costs, when my speed becomes "reckless", what driving without a licence,
-- dangerous or careless driving and drink-driving can cost me.
--
-- SEAT: the rider and the driver. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Is my scooter an eRideable?",
-- "May I ride it on this road?", "How fast may I go on the footpath?", "What is my speed limit?", "How many points does my
-- speeding carry?", "Am I driving at a reckless speed?", "What is the most I can be fined?". Where the law hands a
-- judgment to someone else -- a court's sentence within a range, the CEO's helmet exemption, the Minister's approval of
-- other dimensions for an eRideable -- that judgment is asked as a fact, or the answer is given as the range the court
-- must stay within.
--
-- Provisions covered. Act: s 5 (terms: the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 Part 1 Division 2 supplies them, so
-- that Act's s 4 "motor vehicle", "power assisted pedal cycle" and s 7 "PU" are used); s 49AAA ("above the speed limit",
-- "speed limit"); s 49AB(1) (circumstances of aggravation); s 49(1), (2), (3), (6) (driving while not authorised, its
-- defence and its penalties, arrest without warrant); s 60A (reckless speed); s 60B (penalties for s 60 and s 60A);
-- s 61 (dangerous driving); s 62 (careless driving); s 64 (0.08), s 64AA (0.05), s 64A(1), (2), (4), (5) (0.02),
-- s 64AAA(1), (2) (any blood alcohol). Road Traffic Code 2000: r 3 ("bicycle", "footpath", "path", "default speed
-- limit", "built-up area", "motor vehicle"), r 3A (electric rideable device), r 5 (no infringement notice under 14),
-- r 11(1)-(6) and r 13(2)-(4) (speed limits), r 15 (eRideable speeds), r 17(1), (2) (speeding points and modified
-- penalties), r 210B (eRideables kept off carriageways over 50 km/h), r 212(5), r 215, r 218(1), r 218A, r 223B, r 228(2).
-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Regulations 2014: r 55(2)(h) (no licence needed for an eRideable), r 65(3), (4)
-- (no demerit points on an eRideable). Road Traffic (Vehicles) Regulations 2014: r 15(2)(e) (no vehicle licence for an
-- eRideable). Road Traffic (Administration) Regulations 2014: r 23 (modified penalties for s 49(1), s 62, s 64AA,
-- s 64AAA) and r 24 (the Code's modified penalties apply on an infringement notice).
--
-- Edition. Act: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 48198, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48198.txt; no compilation number stated; its compilation table ends with the Towing
-- Services Act 2024 Pt. 11 Div. 2 (No. 37 of 2024, in force 10 January 2025). Road Traffic Code 2000: version 05-aa0-00,
-- currency start 14 May 2026 (mrdoc 49388, retrieved 19 October 2026), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-code-2000/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49388.txt. Road Traffic (Vehicles) Regulations 2014:
-- version 01-av0-00, currency start 2 October 2026 (mrdoc 49887), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-vehicles-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49887.txt. Road Traffic (Administration)
-- Regulations 2014: version 00-ay0-00, currency start 9 July 2026 (mrdoc 49740), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-administration-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49740.txt. Road Traffic
-- (Authorisation to Drive) Regulations 2014: version 00-ba0-00, currency start 1 July 2026 (mrdoc 49701), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-authorisation-to-drive-regulations-2014/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49701.txt. Road Traffic
-- (Administration) Act 2008 s 4 and s 7 only (mrdoc 48196, retrieved 7 September 2026), deposited at
-- ../../../road-traffic-administration-act-2008/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48196.txt. All are encoded as they stand in
-- those versions; no amendment is unwound.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 49A (caution and necessity permit, beyond the s 49(2)(b) defence), s 50A; s 54 to s 57 (duties after an
-- incident); s 59, s 59A, s 59BA, s 59B (dangerous or careless driving causing death or bodily harm -- the lives cite s 59
-- for speeding, but it is not a speeding offence); s 60 (reckless manner) except through s 60B's penalties; s 61A, s 61B
-- (officers' defences); s 62A to s 62C; s 63 (under the influence), s 64AB to s 64D (drugs); the s 64 to s 64AA offence
-- counts beyond a count the rider states; s 65 to s 73 (testing and evidence); s 71B to s 71H (police disqualification);
-- Part V Division 3 onward (impounding and confiscation, road closures, towing, radar detectors); Parts VII to IX;
-- demerit points beyond the speeding table (they are the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 baseline's);
-- the holiday-period calendar (ATD Regulations r 67 -- asked as a fact); school zone hours, shared zones and other signs
-- beyond a signed limit stated by the driver; the Code's other eRideable and bicycle rules (lights, hook turns, bicycle
-- lanes, keeping left on a path, giving way to pedestrians -- r 213, r 214, r 216, r 217, r 219, r 224, r 229 and others);
-- bicycles and power assisted pedal cycles beyond telling them apart from an eRideable; the Fines, Penalties and
-- Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 (how an infringement notice is paid or contested).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic Act 1974 (WA), with the Road Traffic Code 2000 and the regulations`

§§ `helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 7: "In provisions of a road law dealing with penalties for offences -- (a) these
-- abbreviations are used -- ... PU for penalty unit or penalty units; and (b) a reference to a number of PU is a reference
-- to an amount (in dollars) that is that number multiplied by 50." The Act's s 5 sends the reader to that Act's Part 1
-- Division 2 for its terms.
@export How many dollars is a fine or modified penalty of this many penalty units (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 7)?
GIVEN `penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of penalty units (PU)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars is this many penalty units` IS `penalty units` TIMES 50

§§ `Code r 3A; Administration Act s 4 -- is my device an electric rideable device`

-- Code r 3A(1): "An electric rideable device is a scooter, skateboard, or other vehicle, that -- (a) has at least 1 wheel;
-- and (b) is designed to be used by a single person; and (c) has an electric motor or motors; and (d) is fitted with an
-- effective stopping system controlled by use of brakes, gears or motor control; and (e) when propelled only by the motor
-- or motors, is not capable of going faster than 25 km/h on level ground; and (f) complies with the mass and dimension
-- requirements". (2)(a): "no more than 1 250 mm in length ... no more than 700 mm in width ... no more than 1 350 mm in
-- height ... an unladen mass of no more than 25 kg"; (2)(b): unless the Minister approves other requirements (asked as a
-- fact). (3): it "does not include -- (a) a motorised scooter; or (b) a motorised wheelchair; or (c) an electric personal
-- transporter; or (d) a vehicle with pedals; or (e) a wheeled toy."
-- A vehicle with pedals and a small motor may instead be a "power assisted pedal cycle" (Administration Act s 4: "designed
-- to be propelled through a mechanism operated solely by human power" with auxiliary motors not over a prescribed power),
-- which the Code counts as a "bicycle" (r 3). The prescribed power was not read, so that is not decided here.
DECLARE `My device` HAS
    `it has at least 1 wheel`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is designed for a single person`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has an electric motor`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has an effective stopping system`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `top speed on its motor alone on level ground, in km/h`        IS A NUMBER
    `length in mm`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `width in mm`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `height in mm`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `unladen mass in kg`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `it meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it has pedals`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of device` IS ONE OF
    `an electric rideable device`
    `not an electric rideable device, because it has pedals (it may be a bicycle or power assisted pedal cycle)`
    `not an electric rideable device, because it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`
    `not an electric rideable device, because it does not meet r 3A(1)`

GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`meets the mass and dimension requirements` MEANS
        (    `the device`'s `length in mm` AT MOST 1250
         AND `the device`'s `width in mm` AT MOST 700
         AND `the device`'s `height in mm` AT MOST 1350
         AND `the device`'s `unladen mass in kg` AT MOST 25)
    OR `the device`'s `it meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved`

@export Is my device an electric rideable device (an eRideable) under the Road Traffic Code 2000 r 3A?
GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device` @desc Your device: its wheels, motor, brakes, top speed, size, mass and pedals
GIVETH A `Kind of device`
DECIDE `What kind of device am I riding` IS
    BRANCH IF `the device`'s `it has pedals`
           THEN `not an electric rideable device, because it has pedals (it may be a bicycle or power assisted pedal cycle)`
           IF `the device`'s `it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`
           THEN `not an electric rideable device, because it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`
           IF      `the device`'s `it has at least 1 wheel`
               AND `the device`'s `it is designed for a single person`
               AND `the device`'s `it has an electric motor`
               AND `the device`'s `it has an effective stopping system`
               AND `the device`'s `top speed on its motor alone on level ground, in km/h` AT MOST 25
               AND `meets the mass and dimension requirements` `the device`
           THEN `an electric rideable device`
           OTHERWISE `not an electric rideable device, because it does not meet r 3A(1)`

GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an eRideable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What kind of device am I riding` `the device`
    WHEN `an electric rideable device` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ATD Regulations r 55; Vehicles Regulations r 15; Administration Act s 4 -- licences for an eRideable`

-- ATD Regulations r 55(1): "A person may drive on a road a motor vehicle referred to in subregulation (2) even though the
-- person is not authorised to do so other than by this regulation." (2)(h): "an electric rideable device."
-- So riding an eRideable is driving "authorised under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 Part 2" for
-- s 49(1)(a) of this Act (r 55 is made under that Part, s 11(1) of that Act; INFERENCE as to the link, the ATD Act s 11
-- was read only through the ATD baseline).
@export May I ride my device on a road without a driver's licence, because it is an electric rideable device (Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 55(2)(h))?
GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device` @desc Your device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ride it without a driver's licence` IF `is an eRideable` `the device`

-- Vehicles Regulations r 15(1): "a vehicle licence is required for a vehicle that is a motor vehicle or a trailer." (2): "However,
-- a vehicle licence is not required for a motor vehicle or trailer that is -- ... (e) a motorised scooter or electric rideable
-- device."
@export Does my device need a vehicle licence (registration) (Vehicles Regulations r 15)?
GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device` @desc Your device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my eRideable need a vehicle licence` IF (NOT `is an eRideable` `the device`)

-- Administration Act s 4, "motor vehicle -- ... (b) otherwise, means a selfpropelled vehicle that is not operated on rails and
-- -- ... (ii) does not include a power assisted pedal cycle". This Act takes that meaning (s 5). The Code's own definition
-- ("motor vehicle does not include a motorised wheelchair, motorised scooter, electric rideable device or electric personal
-- transporter", r 3) is for the Code only. ATD Regulations r 55(2)(h) and r 65(4) speak of an eRideable as a "motor
-- vehicle". So this Act's offences for a "motor vehicle" -- dangerous and careless driving, drink-driving -- reach an
-- eRideable rider. INFERENCE from the definitions; no case was searched.
@export Is my electric rideable device a "motor vehicle" for the Road Traffic Act 1974's offences (Administration Act s 4)?
GIVEN `the device` IS A `My device` @desc Your device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my eRideable a motor vehicle for this Act` IF
    `the device`'s `it has an electric motor` AND (NOT `the device`'s `it has pedals`)

§§ `Code r 5, r 228, r 212, r 223B -- who may ride, and how`

-- r 228(2): "A person who is under 16 years of age must not ride an electric rideable device with its motor, or any of its
-- motors, engaged. Modified penalty: 1 PU"
@export Am I old enough to ride an electric rideable device with its motor on (Code r 228(2))?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to ride an eRideable` IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 16

-- r 5: "an alleged offender against these regulations, under 14 years of age, is not to be dealt with by way of an
-- infringement notice and modified penalty."
@export Can I be given an infringement notice for a Road Traffic Code offence (Code r 5)?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the offence was committed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given a Code infringement notice` IF `my age in years` AT LEAST 14

-- r 212(5): "The rider of an electric rideable device must not carry a passenger or animal on the electric rideable device.
-- Modified penalty: 1 PU"
@export May I carry a passenger or an animal on my electric rideable device (Code r 212(5))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I carry a passenger on my eRideable` IS FALSE

-- r 223B(2): "A person must not ride an electric rideable device on a road or path unless the person is wearing a protective
-- helmet (bicycle) or protective helmet (motor cycle) securely fastened on the person's head. Modified penalty: 1 PU".
-- (3): not "(a) a member of a religious or cultural group ... wearing a headdress customarily worn ... if the wearing of that
-- headdress makes it impractical" to wear a helmet; or "(b) ... exempted in writing by the CEO ... for medical reasons, and
-- ... complying with any terms and conditions of that exemption."
@export Must I wear a helmet on my electric rideable device (Code r 223B)?
GIVEN `I wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical
      `the CEO has exempted me in writing for medical reasons and I keep its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO of the Department of Transport has exempted you in writing for medical reasons, and you comply with its terms
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I wear a helmet` IF
        (NOT `I wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical`)
    AND (NOT `the CEO has exempted me in writing for medical reasons and I keep its terms`)

§§ `Code r 210B, r 215, r 218, r 218A, r 15 -- where may I ride my eRideable, and how fast`

-- r 3: "footpath means an area that is open to the public that is designated for, or has as one of its main uses, use by
-- pedestrians"; "path includes bicycle path, footpath, separated footpath and shared path"; "carriageway means a portion of
-- a road that is improved, designed or ordinarily used for vehicular traffic". r 4(2): a rule about a path applies to it
-- only "if the path forms a part of a road" (the Administration Act s 4 "road" includes "every carriageway, footway").
DECLARE `Where I am riding` IS ONE OF
    `a carriageway`
    `a footpath`
    `a shared path`
    `a bicycle path`
    `the pedestrians-only part of a separated footpath`
    `the bicycle part of a separated footpath`

DECLARE `My ride` HAS
    `where I am`                                                          IS A `Where I am riding`
    `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h`                         IS A NUMBER
    `I am only crossing the carriageway, by the shortest safe route`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am only avoiding an obstruction, for no longer than necessary`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I pass a no wheeled devices sign`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a no bicycles sign or marking applies here`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `my speed, in km/h`                                                   IS A NUMBER

-- r 210B(1): "A person must not ride an electric rideable device on a carriageway with a speed limit exceeding 50 km/h."
-- (3): not if "crossing a carriageway ... by the shortest safe route; and ... does not stay on the carriageway longer than
-- necessary". (4): not if "it is necessary to ride on the carriageway to avoid an obstruction; and ... the person does not
-- ride on the carriageway for longer than necessary".
GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`breaks r 210B` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ride`'s `where I am`
    WHEN `a carriageway` THEN
            `the ride`'s `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h` GREATER THAN 50
        AND (NOT `the ride`'s `I am only crossing the carriageway, by the shortest safe route`)
        AND (NOT `the ride`'s `I am only avoiding an obstruction, for no longer than necessary`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- r 215: "The rider of a bicycle or electric rideable device must not ride on a part of a separated footpath designated for
-- the use of pedestrians only." r 218(1): "must not ride on a length of carriageway or path to which a 'no bicycles' sign, or a
-- 'no bicycles' road marking, applies." r 218A: "A person riding an electric rideable device on a road must not travel past a
-- 'no wheeled devices' sign." Nothing in the Code forbids an eRideable on a footpath, shared path or bicycle path; r 15(3)
-- caps its speed on a footpath instead.
@export May I ride my electric rideable device where I am riding (Code r 210B, r 215, r 218, r 218A)?
GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride` @desc Where you are riding, the speed limit, and any signs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ride my eRideable here` IF
        (NOT `breaks r 210B` `the ride`)
    AND (NOT `the ride`'s `I pass a no wheeled devices sign`)
    AND (NOT `the ride`'s `a no bicycles sign or marking applies here`)
    AND CONSIDER `the ride`'s `where I am`
        WHEN `the pedestrians-only part of a separated footpath` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- r 210B(1), "Modified penalty: (a) if the person is riding on a carriageway with a speed limit exceeding 70 km/h -- 10 PU
-- (b) in any other case -- 2 PU". 0 here means no r 210B offence.
@export What is the modified penalty for riding my electric rideable device on this carriageway, in penalty units (Code r 210B)?
GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride` @desc Where you are riding and the speed limit
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for riding my eRideable on this carriageway` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `breaks r 210B` `the ride`) THEN 0
           IF `the ride`'s `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h` GREATER THAN 70 THEN 10
           OTHERWISE 2

-- r 15(1): "This regulation is subject to any other provision of these regulations prescribing a maximum speed for any
-- vehicle lower than that prescribed by this regulation." (2): "on a carriageway, bicycle path or shared path at a speed
-- exceeding 25 km/h." (3): "on a footpath (other than a bicycle path or shared path) at a speed exceeding 10 km/h."
-- The encoder reads both parts of a separated footpath as a "footpath" for r 15(3): the subregulation carves out only a
-- bicycle path and a shared path. On a carriageway the lower signed limit (r 11) governs, by r 15(1).
@export What is the fastest I may ride my electric rideable device where I am, in km/h (Code r 15)?
GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride` @desc Where you are riding and the speed limit
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fastest I may ride my eRideable here` IS
    CONSIDER `the ride`'s `where I am`
    WHEN `a carriageway` THEN `the lesser of` 25 (`the ride`'s `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h`)
    WHEN `a shared path` THEN 25
    WHEN `a bicycle path` THEN 25
    OTHERWISE 10

GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the r 15 cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ride`'s `where I am`
    WHEN `a carriageway` THEN 25
    WHEN `a shared path` THEN 25
    WHEN `a bicycle path` THEN 25
    OTHERWISE 10

-- r 15(2), (3): "Modified penalty: 2 PU". Riding under 25 km/h but over a lower signed limit on a carriageway is instead
-- an offence against r 11 with r 17's modified penalty (non-heavy vehicle) and, on an eRideable, no points (ATD
-- Regulations r 65(4)). 0 here means not speeding.
@export What is the modified penalty for my speed on my electric rideable device, in penalty units (Code r 15, r 11, r 17)?
GIVEN `the ride` IS A `My ride` @desc Where you are riding, the speed limit and your speed
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for my eRideable speed` IS
    BRANCH IF `the ride`'s `my speed, in km/h` GREATER THAN `the r 15 cap` `the ride` THEN 2
           IF `the ride`'s `my speed, in km/h` GREATER THAN `What is the fastest I may ride my eRideable here` `the ride`
           THEN `What is the modified penalty for my speeding`
                    (`the ride`'s `my speed, in km/h` MINUS `the ride`'s `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h`) FALSE
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `Code r 3, r 11, r 13; s 49AAA -- what is my speed limit`

-- r 11(1): "A person must not drive a vehicle at a speed exceeding the default speed limit for that vehicle." (2): "in a
-- built-up area, at a speed exceeding 50 km/h, except within a speed zone in which a higher speed is permitted." (3)-(6): in a
-- speed zone, shared zone, speed limited area or school zone (in its hours), not over the limit applicable to it.
-- r 3: "default speed limit, for a vehicle -- (a) that is limited to a particular speed limit by these regulations that is
-- slower than 110 km/h, means that slower speed limit; or (b) ... means a speed limit of 110 km/h". r 13(2)-(4): towing, a
-- GVM over 12 t, or a bus over 5 t GVM: not over 100 km/h, "notwithstanding the existence of speed zones that permit higher
-- speeds" (r 13(5)). "built-up area" (r 3: street lighting at intervals of not over 100 m for 500 m, or buildings at
-- intervals of less than 100 m for 500 m or more) is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Where I am driving` HAS
    `a sign sets the limit here (speed zone, school zone in its hours, shared zone or speed limited area)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the signed limit, in km/h`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `I am in a built-up area`                                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am towing, over 12 t GVM, or driving a bus over 5 t GVM`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

@export What is my speed limit, in km/h (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 11, r 13)?
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where I am driving` @desc Where you are driving: any signed limit, whether it is a built-up area, and your vehicle
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my speed limit` IS
    LET `the place's limit` MEANS
            IF `where`'s `a sign sets the limit here (speed zone, school zone in its hours, shared zone or speed limited area)`
            THEN `where`'s `the signed limit, in km/h`
            ELSE IF `where`'s `I am in a built-up area` THEN 50 ELSE 110
    IN IF `where`'s `I am towing, over 12 t GVM, or driving a bus over 5 t GVM`
       THEN `the lesser of` 100 `the place's limit`
       ELSE `the place's limit`

-- s 49AAA: "above the speed limit ... means driving the vehicle at a speed that exceeds the speed limit applicable to the
-- driver, the vehicle or the length of road where it is being driven". 0 here means not above it.
@export By how many km/h am I above the speed limit (s 49AAA)?
GIVEN `my speed` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed in km/h
      `my speed limit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed limit in km/h
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many km/h am I above the speed limit` IS `the greater of` 0 (`my speed` MINUS `my speed limit`)

§§ `Code r 17; ATD Regulations r 65(3), (4); Administration Regulations r 24 -- what my speeding costs`

-- r 17(1), "Exceeding a speed limit by --": (a) "not more than 9 km/h": no points, 2 PU; (b) "more than 9 km/h but not more
-- than 19 km/h": 4 points in a holiday period, otherwise 2; 4 PU; (c) "more than 19 km/h but not more than 29 km/h": 6 / 3;
-- 8 PU; (d) "more than 29 km/h but not more than 40 km/h": 12 / 6; 16 PU; (e) "more than 40 km/h": 14 / 7; 24 PU.
-- r 17(2), "if the offence is committed by the driver of a heavy vehicle": the same points; 4, 6, 10, 24 and 30 PU.
-- ATD Regulations r 65(3) makes those points the demerit points; r 65(4): "an offence that is committed by a person driving or
-- using a motor vehicle that is a motorised scooter or electric rideable device is not a demerit point offence."
-- Administration Regulations r 24(2): on an infringement notice "the penalty ... is the modified penalty that the road law
-- specifies". The holiday period (ATD Regulations r 67) is asked as a fact.
-- The same figures, under the same names, are in the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 baseline.
@export How many demerit points does my speeding carry (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17; Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 65(3), (4))?
GIVEN `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was in a holiday period (long weekend, Easter, Christmas)
      `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were riding a motorised scooter or an electric rideable device
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many demerit points does my speeding carry` IS
    BRANCH IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
           IF `on a motorised scooter or electric rideable device` THEN 0
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 9 THEN 0
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 19 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 4 ELSE 2)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 29 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 6 ELSE 3)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 40 THEN (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 12 ELSE 6)
           OTHERWISE (IF `in a holiday period` THEN 14 ELSE 7)

@export What is the modified penalty for my speeding, in penalty units (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17)?
GIVEN `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `driving a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a heavy vehicle (GCM 22.5 t or more)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for my speeding` IS
    BRANCH IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 9 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 4 ELSE 2)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 19 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 6 ELSE 4)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 29 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 10 ELSE 8)
           IF `km/h over the limit` AT MOST 40 THEN (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 24 ELSE 16)
           OTHERWISE (IF `driving a heavy vehicle` THEN 30 ELSE 24)

-- Code r 9(2): a Code offence that goes to court is "liable -- (a) for a first offence, to a penalty not exceeding 64 penalty
-- units (64 PU); and (b) for a subsequent offence, to a penalty not exceeding 96 penalty units (96 PU)" -- a subsequent
-- offence being any earlier offence "of any kind against these regulations" (r 9(3)). (Part 16 Division 2 and r 244 differ,
-- r 9(1A); not encoded.)
@export What is the most a court can fine me for a Road Traffic Code offence such as speeding, in penalty units (Code r 9(2))?
GIVEN `I have committed a Code offence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed any offence against the Road Traffic Code before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most a court can fine me for a Code offence` IS
    IF `I have committed a Code offence before` THEN 96 ELSE 64

§§ `s 49AB, s 60A, s 60B -- reckless speed`

-- s 49AB(1): "a person commits an offence in circumstances of aggravation if at the time of the alleged offence -- (a) the
-- person was unlawfully driving the vehicle concerned without the consent of the owner ...; or (aa) the person has never held a
-- prescribed authorisation; or (ab) ... is a person described in section 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da); or (ac) ... the
-- prescribed authorisation does not authorise the person to drive a vehicle of the kind concerned; or (ad) the person commits
-- an offence under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 section 38(1); or (b) the person was driving the vehicle
-- concerned on a road at 30 km/h or more above the speed limit; or (c) the person was driving the vehicle concerned to escape
-- pursuit by a police officer."
DECLARE `My driving` HAS
    `I was driving without the owner's consent`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have never held a licence or permit`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a person described in s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da)`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `my licence does not cover this kind of vehicle`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am committing an offence under the ATD Act s 38(1)`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `km/h above the speed limit`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `I was driving to escape pursuit by a police officer`                      IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I committing a driving offence in circumstances of aggravation (s 49AB(1))?
GIVEN `the driving` IS A `My driving` @desc How you were driving, and your licence position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I driving in circumstances of aggravation` IF
        `the driving`'s `I was driving without the owner's consent`
    OR  `the driving`'s `I have never held a licence or permit`
    OR  `the driving`'s `I am a person described in s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da)`
    OR  `the driving`'s `my licence does not cover this kind of vehicle`
    OR  `the driving`'s `I am committing an offence under the ATD Act s 38(1)`
    OR  `the driving`'s `km/h above the speed limit` AT LEAST 30
    OR  `the driving`'s `I was driving to escape pursuit by a police officer`

-- s 60A(1): "A person commits an offence if the person drives a motor vehicle at a speed of 155 km/h or more on any other
-- length of road." (2): "... at 45 km/h or more above the speed limit -- (a) in a confiscation zone; or (b) on any other length
-- of road." (The words "any other" pair each offence with its confiscation-zone twin; both are offences. s 61B's defences for
-- police, fire, rescue and ambulance drivers are not encoded.)
@export Am I driving at a reckless speed (s 60A)?
GIVEN `my speed` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed in km/h
      `my speed limit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed limit in km/h
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I driving at a reckless speed` IF
    `my speed` AT LEAST 155 OR `By how many km/h am I above the speed limit` `my speed` `my speed limit` AT LEAST 45

-- s 60B(2): "(a) for a first offence, to a fine of 120 PU or to imprisonment for 9 months; and (b) for a second offence, to a
-- fine of 180 PU or to imprisonment for 9 months; and (c) for a third or subsequent offence, to a fine of 240 PU or to
-- imprisonment for 12 months." (3): disqualified "(a) ... not less than 6 months ... (b) ... not less than 12 months ... (c)
-- ... permanently". (4), (5): escaping pursuit (s 49AB(1)(c)) makes it a crime -- "imprisonment for 5 years", at least 6
-- months not suspended, and disqualification "not less than 2 years" for a first or second offence, permanent for a third.
@export What is the most I can be fined for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in penalty units (s 60B(2))?
GIVEN `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for reckless driving or speed` IS
    BRANCH IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 120
           IF `which offence of mine this is` EQUALS 2 THEN 180
           OTHERWISE 240

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in months (s 60B(2), (4))?
GIVEN `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for reckless driving or speed` IS
    BRANCH IF `I was escaping police pursuit` THEN 60
           IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 2 THEN 9
           OTHERWISE 12

-- Returns 0 where the disqualification must be permanent; ask `Must I be permanently disqualified` for that.
@export What is the shortest disqualification a court must order for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in months (s 60B(3), (5))?
GIVEN `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the shortest disqualification for reckless driving or speed` IS
    BRANCH IF `which offence of mine this is` AT LEAST 3 THEN 0
           IF `I was escaping police pursuit` THEN 24
           IF `which offence of mine this is` EQUALS 2 THEN 12
           OTHERWISE 6

@export Must I be permanently disqualified for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed (s 60B(3)(c), (5)(d))?
GIVEN `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be permanently disqualified` IF `which offence of mine this is` AT LEAST 3

§§ `s 61, s 62 -- dangerous and careless driving`

-- s 61(1): "Every person who drives a motor vehicle in a manner (which expression includes speed) that is, having regard to
-- all the circumstances of the case, dangerous to the public or to any person commits an offence." Whether it was dangerous is
-- the court's judgment, so it is the premise of the penalty questions, not decided here.
-- s 61(3): "(a) unless paragraph (b) applies -- (i) for a first offence -- to a fine of 60 PU; (ii) for a subsequent offence --
-- to a fine of 120 PU or to imprisonment for 9 months; and, in any event, ... disqualified ... for a period of not less than 12
-- months; (b) if ... committed in the circumstance of aggravation referred to in section 49AB(1)(c) -- to a fine of 720 PU or
-- to imprisonment for 3 years; and ... not less than 2 years." (4): an earlier offence against s 59, 59A, 60 or 60A counts as an
-- earlier s 61 offence. (The "in any event" disqualification is read as attaching to a subsequent offence only, the reading the
-- paragraph's layout gives; INFERENCE.)
@export What is the most I can be fined for dangerous driving, in penalty units (s 61(3), (4))?
GIVEN `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier offences you have committed against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for dangerous driving` IS
    BRANCH IF `I was escaping police pursuit` THEN 720
           IF `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` AT LEAST 1 THEN 120
           OTHERWISE 60

@export What is the shortest disqualification a court must order for dangerous driving, in months (s 61(3))?
GIVEN `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier offences you have committed against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the shortest disqualification for dangerous driving` IS
    BRANCH IF `I was escaping police pursuit` THEN 24
           IF `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` AT LEAST 1 THEN 12
           OTHERWISE 0

-- s 62: "Every person who drives a motor vehicle without due care and attention commits an offence. Penalty: a fine of 30 PU."
-- Administration Regulations r 23 Table: "s. 62 Careless driving 6" (PU, if dealt with by infringement notice).
@export What is the modified penalty for careless driving if I get an infringement notice, in penalty units (s 62; Administration Regulations r 23)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for careless driving` IS 6

@export What is the most a court can fine me for careless driving, in penalty units (s 62)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for careless driving` IS 30

§§ `s 49; Administration Regulations r 23 -- driving without a licence`

-- s 49(1): "A person who -- (a) drives a motor vehicle on a road while not authorised under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to
-- Drive) Act 2008 Part 2 to do so ... commits an offence." (2): "It is a defence ... to prove that the motor vehicle was driven
-- in accordance with -- (a) regulations referred to in the [ATD Act] section 11(1); or (b) a necessity permit under section
-- 49A." Whether I am authorised is the ATD Act's question (its baseline's `Am I authorised to drive`); it is asked here as a
-- fact, except that an eRideable rider is authorised by ATD Regulations r 55(2)(h).
-- s 49(3): the police may arrest without warrant, and the heavier penalties apply, if the person "(a) ... has applied for, but
-- has been refused, an Australian driver licence ...; or (b) ... is disqualified ...; or (ca) ... has held an Australian driver
-- licence of a kind required but ceased to hold [it] other than ... voluntarily surrendered ... expired ... [or penalty
-- enforcement]; or (c) whose authority to drive ... is for the time being suspended ...; or (da) [a prescribed class]; or (d)
-- who is no longer authorised to drive because of penalty enforcement laws". s 49(4) (a pending review) is folded into the
-- rider's answer.
DECLARE `Why I am not authorised` IS ONE OF
    `I never held a licence of the kind needed, or it expired or I surrendered it`
    `I am a type 1A novice driving between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit`
    `I lost my licence under penalty enforcement laws (s 49(3)(d))`
    `I was refused, disqualified, cancelled or suspended, or am in a prescribed class (s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c), (da))`

DECLARE `My unlicensed drive` HAS
    `I was riding an electric rideable device`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 to drive this vehicle`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I drove under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `why I am not authorised`                                                            IS A `Why I am not authorised`
    `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)`                                         IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I commit an offence by driving without a licence or authorisation (s 49(1), (2); Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 55)?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Your vehicle, your authorisation and why you lack it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` IF
        (NOT `the drive`'s `I was riding an electric rideable device`)
    AND (NOT `the drive`'s `I am authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 to drive this vehicle`)
    AND (NOT `the drive`'s `I drove under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit`)

GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the drive`'s `why I am not authorised`
    WHEN `I was refused, disqualified, cancelled or suspended, or am in a prescribed class (s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c), (da))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls in s 49(3)(d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the drive`'s `why I am not authorised`
    WHEN `I lost my licence under penalty enforcement laws (s 49(3)(d))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 49(1) "Penalty for this subsection: (a) unless subsection (3) applies -- (i) for a first offence, 6 PU; (ii) for a
-- subsequent offence, 12 PU; (b) if subsection (3)(d), but no other paragraph of subsection (3), applies -- (i) a fine of not
-- less than 4 PU or more than 30 PU; and (ii) imprisonment for not more than 12 months, and the court may order that the
-- offender be disqualified ... for ... not more than 3 years; (c) if subsection (3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da) applies -- (i)
-- for a first offence, a fine of not less than 8 PU or more than 40 PU, and imprisonment for not more than 12 months; (ii) for a
-- subsequent offence, a fine of not less than 20 PU or more than 80 PU, and imprisonment for not more than 18 months, and the
-- court shall order that the offender be disqualified ... for a period of not less than 9 months and not more than 3 years."
@export What is the most I can be fined for driving without a licence, in penalty units (s 49(1))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised, and whether you have done it before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for driving unlicensed` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive`) THEN 0
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` `the drive` THEN (IF `the drive`'s `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` THEN 80 ELSE 40)
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(d)` `the drive` THEN 30
           OTHERWISE (IF `the drive`'s `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` THEN 12 ELSE 6)

@export What is the least a court must fine me for driving without a licence, in penalty units (s 49(1))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised, and whether you have done it before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the least I can be fined for driving unlicensed` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive`) THEN 0
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` `the drive` THEN (IF `the drive`'s `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` THEN 20 ELSE 8)
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(d)` `the drive` THEN 4
           OTHERWISE 0

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for driving without a licence, in months (s 49(1))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised, and whether you have done it before
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for driving unlicensed` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive`) THEN 0
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` `the drive` THEN (IF `the drive`'s `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` THEN 18 ELSE 12)
           IF `falls in s 49(3)(d)` `the drive` THEN 12
           OTHERWISE 0

@export Must the court disqualify me (for 9 months to 3 years) for driving without a licence (s 49(1) penalty (c))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be disqualified for driving unlicensed` IF
    `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive` AND `falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` `the drive`

@export May the police arrest me without a warrant for driving without a licence (s 49(3))?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be arrested without a warrant for driving unlicensed` IF
    `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive`
    AND (`falls in s 49(3)(a) to (da)` `the drive` OR `falls in s 49(3)(d)` `the drive`)

-- Administration Regulations r 23 Table, s 49(1): 2 PU if "(a) the offence is not committed by a novice driver (type 1A)
-- between midnight and the following 5 a.m. or in relation to the number of passengers ...; and (b) the Road Traffic Act 1974
-- s. 49(3) does not apply"; 4 PU "if the offence is committed by a novice driver (type 1A) either -- (a) between midnight and
-- the following 5 a.m.; or (b) in relation to the number of passengers". Otherwise no infringement notice may be given: the
-- matter goes to court (0 here).
@export What is the modified penalty if I am given an infringement notice for driving without a licence, in penalty units (Administration Regulations r 23)?
GIVEN `the drive` IS A `My unlicensed drive` @desc Why you were not authorised
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for driving unlicensed` IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` `the drive`) THEN 0
           OTHERWISE
              CONSIDER `the drive`'s `why I am not authorised`
              WHEN `I never held a licence of the kind needed, or it expired or I surrendered it` THEN 2
              WHEN `I am a type 1A novice driving between midnight and 5 a.m. or over the passenger limit` THEN 4
              OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA -- drink-driving`

-- s 64(1): "drives or attempts to drive a motor vehicle while having a blood alcohol content of or above 0.08 g of alcohol per
-- 100 ml of blood". s 64AA(1): "of or above 0.05". s 64A(1): "A person to whom this subsection applies ... of or above 0.02";
-- (2): it applies to a person who "(a) is a novice driver as defined in the [ATD Act] section 40(2); or ... (c) is subject to
-- an order disqualifying [them] ... for an offence against section 63, 67 or 67AD(6), or for a second or subsequent offence
-- against section 64 ...; or (d) [licence cancelled after such an order]; or (e) holds an extraordinary licence ...; or (f) is a
-- recently disqualified driver; or (g) [a prescribed class]". (4), (5): also any driver of a bus seating more than 12 carrying
-- passengers, a vehicle carrying passengers for hire or reward, a vehicle with a GCM of 22.5 t or more, or a prescribed
-- dangerous goods vehicle. s 64AAA(1), (2): those same persons and vehicles, "while having any blood alcohol content".
-- The answer is the highest of these the reading reaches (a charge under a higher section may end in conviction under a lower
-- one, s 64(4), s 64AA(3)). The s 64AAA(3) defence (alcohol not from drink or a substance taken to consume alcohol) is not
-- encoded.
DECLARE `Blood alcohol offence` IS ONE OF
    `no blood alcohol offence`
    `s 64AAA: any blood alcohol, where none is allowed`
    `s 64A: 0.02 or above, where that is my limit`
    `s 64AA: 0.05 or above`
    `s 64: 0.08 or above`

DECLARE `My drinking and driving` HAS
    `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL`                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `I am a novice driver (ATD Act s 40(2))`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists (drink-driving disqualification, extraordinary licence, recently disqualified)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists (bus with passengers, hire passengers, GCM 22.5 t or more, dangerous goods)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no alcohol is allowed` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `I am a novice driver (ATD Act s 40(2))`
    OR  `the facts`'s `I am otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists (drink-driving disqualification, extraordinary licence, recently disqualified)`
    OR  `the facts`'s `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists (bus with passengers, hire passengers, GCM 22.5 t or more, dangerous goods)`

@export Which blood alcohol offence, if any, do I commit by driving (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving` @desc Your blood alcohol content, and whether you or your vehicle must have none
GIVETH A `Blood alcohol offence`
DECIDE `Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` IS
    BRANCH IF `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` AT LEAST 0.08 THEN `s 64: 0.08 or above`
           IF `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` AT LEAST 0.05 THEN `s 64AA: 0.05 or above`
           IF `no alcohol is allowed` `the facts` AND `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` AT LEAST 0.02
           THEN `s 64A: 0.02 or above, where that is my limit`
           IF `no alcohol is allowed` `the facts` AND `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` GREATER THAN 0
           THEN `s 64AAA: any blood alcohol, where none is allowed`
           OTHERWISE `no blood alcohol offence`

-- s 64(2) Table, "First offence / Second offence / Subsequent offence", Min / Max / Disq:
--   >= 0.08 but < 0.09: 15 PU 45 PU 6 months | 32 PU 45 PU 8 months | 32 PU 45 PU 10 months
--   >= 0.09 but < 0.11: 17 PU 45 PU 7 months | 34 PU 45 PU 10 months | 34 PU 45 PU 13 months
--   >= 0.11 but < 0.13: 20 PU 45 PU 8 months | 36 PU 60 PU 14 months | 36 PU 60 PU 17 months
--   >= 0.13:            23 PU 45 PU 9 months | 48 PU 75 PU 18 months | 48 PU 90 PU 30 months
-- s 64AA(2): a first offence, "a fine of not more than 25 PU" (no minimum, no compulsory disqualification); (2a) Table, second
-- / subsequent: >= 0.05 but < 0.07: 25-40 PU, 6 / 8 months; >= 0.07: 30-40 PU, 8 / 10 months.
-- s 64A(1), (4): "a fine of not less than 8 PU or more than 15 PU; and ... disqualified ... for not less than 3 months."
-- s 64AAA(1), (2): "a fine of not less than 8 PU or more than 15 PU" (no disqualification).
-- Which offence of mine this is counts earlier offences that the section deems to be offences against it (s 64(3), s 64AA(2c));
-- the rider states the count.
GIVEN `the bac` IS A NUMBER
      `low` IS A NUMBER
      `mid` IS A NUMBER
      `high` IS A NUMBER
      `top` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`by s 64 band` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the bac` LESS THAN 0.09 THEN `low`
           IF `the bac` LESS THAN 0.11 THEN `mid`
           IF `the bac` LESS THAN 0.13 THEN `high`
           OTHERWISE `top`

@export What is the least a court must fine me for drink-driving, in penalty units (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving` @desc Your blood alcohol content, and whether you or your vehicle must have none
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence under this section, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the least I can be fined for drink-driving` IS
    LET `bac` MEANS `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL`
    IN CONSIDER `Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` `the facts`
       WHEN `s 64: 0.08 or above` THEN
            IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN `by s 64 band` `bac` 15 17 20 23
                                                       ELSE `by s 64 band` `bac` 32 34 36 48
       WHEN `s 64AA: 0.05 or above` THEN
            IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 0 ELSE IF `bac` LESS THAN 0.07 THEN 25 ELSE 30
       WHEN `s 64A: 0.02 or above, where that is my limit` THEN 8
       WHEN `s 64AAA: any blood alcohol, where none is allowed` THEN 8
       OTHERWISE 0

@export What is the most I can be fined for drink-driving, in penalty units (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving` @desc Your blood alcohol content, and whether you or your vehicle must have none
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence under this section, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for drink-driving` IS
    LET `bac` MEANS `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL`
    IN CONSIDER `Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` `the facts`
       WHEN `s 64: 0.08 or above` THEN
            BRANCH IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 45
                   IF `which offence of mine this is` EQUALS 2 THEN `by s 64 band` `bac` 45 45 60 75
                   OTHERWISE `by s 64 band` `bac` 45 45 60 90
       WHEN `s 64AA: 0.05 or above` THEN
            IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 25 ELSE 40
       WHEN `s 64A: 0.02 or above, where that is my limit` THEN 15
       WHEN `s 64AAA: any blood alcohol, where none is allowed` THEN 15
       OTHERWISE 0

@export What is the shortest disqualification a court must order for drink-driving, in months (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving` @desc Your blood alcohol content, and whether you or your vehicle must have none
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence under this section, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the shortest disqualification for drink-driving` IS
    LET `bac` MEANS `the facts`'s `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL`
    IN CONSIDER `Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` `the facts`
       WHEN `s 64: 0.08 or above` THEN
            BRANCH IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN `by s 64 band` `bac` 6 7 8 9
                   IF `which offence of mine this is` EQUALS 2 THEN `by s 64 band` `bac` 8 10 14 18
                   OTHERWISE `by s 64 band` `bac` 10 13 17 30
       WHEN `s 64AA: 0.05 or above` THEN
            BRANCH IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 0
                   IF `which offence of mine this is` EQUALS 2 THEN (IF `bac` LESS THAN 0.07 THEN 6 ELSE 8)
                   OTHERWISE (IF `bac` LESS THAN 0.07 THEN 8 ELSE 10)
       WHEN `s 64A: 0.02 or above, where that is my limit` THEN 3
       OTHERWISE 0

-- Administration Regulations r 23 Table: "s. 64AA A first offence of driving or attempting to drive a motor vehicle while
-- having a blood alcohol content of or above 0.05 g ... 20"; "s. 64AAA Driving or attempting to drive a motor vehicle while
-- having any blood alcohol content 8". No other drink-driving offence is in the table, so it goes to court (0 here). A
-- reading of 0.08 or above is charged under s 64 and is not in the table (INFERENCE that it will be charged so).
@export What is the modified penalty if I am given an infringement notice for drink-driving, in penalty units (Administration Regulations r 23)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My drinking and driving` @desc Your blood alcohol content, and whether you or your vehicle must have none
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence under this section, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the modified penalty for drink-driving` IS
    CONSIDER `Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` `the facts`
    WHEN `s 64AA: 0.05 or above` THEN (IF `which offence of mine this is` AT MOST 1 THEN 20 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `s 64AAA: any blood alcohol, where none is allowed` THEN 8
    OTHERWISE 0
